WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.319
When a download finishes, you can check that the file wasn't changed or corrupted.

2
00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:08.951
Open the download details and find the checksum section.

3
00:00:08.951 --> 00:00:11.091
Click Compute to start the check.

4
00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:15.761
Arus reads the saved file and calculates the S H A, two fifty-six, code.

5
00:00:15.761 --> 00:00:18.356
This can take a moment for a large file.

6
00:00:18.356 --> 00:00:21.793
When it's done, the code appears on the details page.

7
00:00:21.793 --> 00:00:25.880
Copy it and compare it with the code from the file's publisher.

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.317
If they match, the file is identical and safe to use.

9
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:33.533
Save the matching code as a note, especially for important files.

10
00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:37.879
If they differ, the file may be damaged or changed during download.

11
00:00:37.879 --> 00:00:42.095
This check is useful for installers, archives, or work documents.

12
00:00:42.095 --> 00:00:45.598
Most importantly, the process runs locally on your PC.

13
00:00:45.598 --> 00:00:48.062
No file or code is sent to any server.

14
00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:51.435
So you can check sensitive files with peace of mind.

